================================================================================
SCOPE — please read before reusing
================================================================================

The MIT terms above cover our own contributions: the reweighting schemes and
imbalance-aware losses, the loss landscape diagnostics, the analysis and figure
scripts at the repository root, and the modifications made to both upstream
codebases.

This repository bundles two independent codebases derived from different
upstream projects, under DIFFERENT licences. The repository as a whole is not
uniformly MIT.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
KPConv-PyTorch/ — MIT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Derived from KPConv-PyTorch by Hugues Thomas
https://github.com/HuguesTHOMAS/KPConv-PyTorch
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2019 HuguesTHOMAS.

Fully MIT-licensed. Full text and third-party notices in KPConv-PyTorch/LICENSE.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RandLA-Net/ — CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 applies to inherited components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Derived from the PyTorch port at
https://github.com/liuxuexun/RandLA-Net-Pytorch-New (declared MIT), which builds
on https://github.com/qiqihaer/RandLA-Net-pytorch and copies components from the
official TensorFlow implementation
https://github.com/QingyongHu/RandLA-Net, released under
Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International.

A downstream project can license its own contributions but cannot relicense code
it copied. Components originating in the official implementation therefore
REMAIN under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, which:

  - restricts use to non-commercial purposes, and
  - requires derivative works to be shared under the same terms.

The full licence text is retained at RandLA-Net/license.txt. Anyone reusing that
half of this repository should treat CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 as the binding constraint.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components used by both halves
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

loss-landscape — Hao Li, Zheng Xu, Gavin Taylor, Christoph Studer, Tom Goldstein
https://github.com/tomgoldstein/loss-landscape
MIT License. The filter-normalised weight perturbation approach used in the
diagnostics scripts of both halves follows this work ("Visualizing the Loss
Landscape of Neural Nets", NeurIPS 2018).

nanoflann — Jose Luis Blanco-Claraco and contributors
https://github.com/jlblancoc/nanoflann
BSD 2-Clause License. The full licence text is retained in the headers of
KPConv-PyTorch/cpp_wrappers/cpp_utils/nanoflann/nanoflann.hpp,
RandLA-Net/utils/cpp_wrappers/cpp_utils/nanoflann/nanoflann.hpp and
RandLA-Net/utils/nearest_neighbors/nanoflann.hpp, and must be kept intact.
